<section id="office"><h2>Garage office, left of the house door</h2>
<p>A finished 6.5×5.5 ft room (~36 sf) on the gym side of the house door. The 3 ft walkway to the door and the basement stair stays clear. There is no exterior window here and no loft. The basement secret office keeps the glass desk and Aeron; this room gets a simple 30×60″ desk, a mesh task chair, and a monitor arm.</p>
<div class="fig2"><figure><a href="img/office-plan.jpg"><img loading="lazy" src="img/office-plan.jpg" alt="Office plan, to scale"></a><figcaption>Office plan, to scale: 6.5×5.5 ft room, door and sidelight to the walkway, 30×60″ desk, 9k mini-split, power and data at the desk</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="img/office-garage-1.jpg"><img loading="lazy" src="img/office-garage-1.jpg" alt="Concept: the office built on the gym side of the house door, walkway kept clear"></a><figcaption>Concept: the office built on the gym side of the house door, walkway kept clear</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="full"><figure><a href="img/office-garage-2.jpg"><img loading="lazy" src="img/office-garage-2.jpg" alt="Office interior concept"></a><figcaption>Office interior concept: desk, dual monitors, solid-core door with a sidelight, wall-head mini-split. Borrowed light only — no exterior window.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Build-out</h3><ul>
<li><b>Walls:</b> 2×4, mineral-wool batts, 5/8″ drywall. The gym-facing wall gets two layers of 5/8″ drywall with Green Glue or equivalent, for sound isolation.</li>
<li><b>Door:</b> solid-core (or acoustic) door with a sweep and weatherstripping, plus a narrow laminated-glass sidelight for borrowed light.</li>
<li><b>Ceiling:</b> a finished drywall lid at about 8 ft, insulated above, under the sloped garage ceiling (about 10–11 ft at this wall). That lid helps contain gym noise.</li>
<li><b>HVAC:</b> a 9,000 BTU cold-climate wall head, or a second head on the gym 24k multi-zone, independent of the open garage. Condenser on the south wall, off the septic.</li>
<li><b>Power / data:</b> two 20A circuits, outlets at the desk, hardwired Ethernet to the house, a ceiling light, and a CO alarm (required in a closed garage room).</li>
<li><b>Sound:</b> with the door closed, Zoom and calls should be workable. It will not be a recording studio; gym noise will still leak.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Cost</h3>
<p>About <b>$4,000 low / $9,000 likely / $16,000 high</b>, including a separate mini-split head and a simple desk setup, not including the gym unit or the garage subpanel. Confirm the house-door swing and the stair half-wall on site before framing.</p>
</div></div></section>

